// A constant above 16 bits needs ldi + ldih, and emitting one without the
// other is the mistake vm-abi.md warns a code generator about.
//
// The last two lines are the same 32 bits printed both ways: `print` is signed
// because every comparison this language emits is signed, and `printu` is the
// raw form a device reading comes back as.
// expect: 65535
// expect: 65536
// expect: 305419896
// expect: -1
// expect: 4294967295
println(65535)
println(65536)
println(0x12345678)
println(0 - 1)
printu(0 - 1)
println("")
